  55: ### The root cause is not the cast â€” it is that two statements never meet
  56: 
  57: The cast is the symptom. The cause is that the suite's declaration and the adapter's
  58: implementation are **two independent claims with no link between them**:
  59: 
  60: - `tests/at/suites/req-016/_bind.ts:23` says "my system under test is a `NotificationsSut` and my
  61:   world is a `World`".
  62: - `tests/at/suites/req-016/_fixture.ts:211` says `const sut: NotificationsSut = { â€¦ }` and
  63:   `class NotificationFixtureWorld implements World` â€” statically checked, **but only against
  64:   itself**.
  65: 
  66: The link is severed in `tests/at/harness/index.ts:36-54`: `loadAdapter` imports the adapter
  67: dynamically and casts the module to `Partial<FixtureAdapterModule>`, whose `sut` is
  68: `Record<string, unknown>`. Every type the producer proved is discarded at that boundary, and the
  69: consumer then invents its own.
  70: 
  71: This is exactly the failure shape the way of work names as the one it exists to delete: **a
  72: declared fact drifting from a real fact with nothing able to detect the gap.** Today a suite can
  73: write `bindSuite<AnythingAtAll, AnythingAtAll>` and `bun run typecheck` stays green.
